# Docs & Artifact Sync (Definition of Done)

An implementation is **incomplete** until the as-built docs and (when applicable) the
shipped artifact match the code. Do this after code + tests, before claiming done.

**Do not wait for the user to ask.** Syncing `PRD.md` / `project_context.md` and rebuilding
`BoWFM.html` is part of the same turn as the code change — not a follow-up the user must
request.

## When this applies

Any change that affects product behavior, UI, engine logic, types, build scripts,
defaults, DQ rules, tests that change expected behavior, or the shipped artifact.

**UI-only JSX reorders still count** — if it ships in the bundle, run
`npm run build:standalone` and `npm run check:artifact`.

## Working directory

If the Cursor workspace is the parent folder (`Bo_4Final-main (2)/`) rather than the app
repo, run all npm commands from `Bo_4Final-main/` (where `package.json` and `src/` live).
`BoWFM.html` is written at that app root.

## Mandatory order

1. **Code + tests** — existing rules still apply (offline contract, frozen HC chain,
   testing protocol).
2. **Update `PRD.md`** — as-built, not aspirational:
   - Behavior / UI / requirements → relevant §1–§10
   - New limitation → §10
   - New or resolved backlog item → §11 (same P0 / P1 / P2 / G ID style; remove resolved)
   - Bump Version / Date in the header table when product behavior changes
3. **Update `project_context.md`**:
   - Architecture / getting-started / commands → §2–§4
   - Engine / search behavior → §5
   - New frozen decision → §6
   - Conventions / testing → §8–§9
   - New common workflow → §10
   - Drift risks, open items, recently fixed → §11
4. **Rebuild the deliverable** when `src/`, `scripts/build-standalone.mts`,
   Vite / Tailwind / build config, or anything that reaches the bundle changed:

```bash
npm run build:standalone
```

Confirm `BoWFM.html` at the app root is updated (mtime ≥ newest watched source).
Do not skip for "small" UI/engine fixes — that file **is** the product. Never weaken
`scripts/build-standalone.mts` offline guards to make the build pass.

5. **Gate** — run `npm run check:artifact` (also runs at the end of `npm test`).
   A project `stop` hook (`.cursor/hooks/ensure-artifact-fresh.mjs`) will follow up
   automatically if you try to finish with a stale `BoWFM.html`.

## Explicit skips

- Pure doc / rule edits with no code or build impact → update docs only; no rebuild
- Questions / exploration with no implementation → no doc or artifact churn

## Completion check

Before finishing, state which of the three were updated (`PRD.md`, `project_context.md`,
`BoWFM.html`), or why the rebuild was skipped. If you rebuilt, mention that
`npm run check:artifact` passed.
